<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-01--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2023-agential-01: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.33";
    dc:description "Restricted inverse morphogenesis problems are empirically and computationally testable. The universal impossibility and counterfactual historical comparison in the claim are not resolvable from existing datasets and lack a unique empirical consequence.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: One could benchmark inverse-design success for specified developmental models and target anatomies, but finite failures cannot establish that the general inverse problem is unsolvable or that this, rather than germline access, historically limits Lamarckian inheritance.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'In general unsolvable' is not falsified by successes in selected systems.", "Computational difficulty and biological historical limitation are conflated.", "Full-scale Lamarckism is not a measurable endpoint.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.77"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.327"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-01--gpt--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2023-agential-01 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 0.3";
